findings.body:
The emitter now assigns `<remarks>` to `operation.Summary`:

::diff{file="src/OpenApi/gen/XmlCommentGenerator.Emitter.cs" lines="372-384"}

In the OpenAPI model, `Summary` is the short title and `Description` is the long-form text. `<remarks>` is long-form by definition. With this change, any method that has both `<summary>` and `<remarks>` loses its summary, because the remarks overwrite it. The `Description` slot then only gets the `<description>` value, or nothing. Multi-paragraph remarks also end up in the short title field that UIs like Swagger/Scalar render on one line.

The PR description doesn't mention this, and it's unrelated to the null-reference fix. Every checked-in snapshot still contains `operation.Description = remarks;`, so the snapshot tests will fail against this emitter.

::suggestion{file="src/OpenApi/gen/XmlCommentGenerator.Emitter.cs" lines="380-383"}
                if (methodComment.Remarks is { } remarks)
                {
                    operation.Description = remarks;
                }

`operation.RequestBody.Description = description;` used to run before the example block. Now it runs after it:

::diff{file="src/OpenApi/gen/XmlCommentGenerator.Emitter.cs" lines="462-482"}

Inside the example block there is an early `continue` that fires when `operation.RequestBody.Content` is null. If a property has an `<example>` and the request body has no content map, the loop now skips the description assignment completely. The old code always set it. The PR description doesn't explain the change, and it has nothing to do with the null fix. The new snapshot still shows the original order, so the snapshot test will also fail on this hunk.

::suggestion{file="src/OpenApi/gen/XmlCommentGenerator.Emitter.cs" lines="464-480"}
